WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.910
A length of wire, a power supply,
an ammeter and a voltmeter:

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.230
the simplest circuit in physics.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.290
Turn up the potential difference, and
the current through the wire rises.

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.030
It sounds obvious: twice
the potential difference,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.520
twice the current.

6
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.450
But is that always true?

7
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.160
When does the current exactly double?

8
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.420
In this mission, you'll define resistance,

9
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.240
and see what it does to the current
at a fixed potential difference.

10
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.650
Then you'll go inside the metal, and
find out where resistance actually comes

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.460
from.

12
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.930
Your mission: find out when doubling
the potential difference exactly doubles

13
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:36.680
the current.
